        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "This is a timing-side-channel vulnerability in a third-party JSON parsing library (json.hpp). The library compares MACs/digests using == operator instead of constant-time comparison, which can leak information about the values being compared through timing analysis. This is classified as a low-impact issue (C rating) because it's a timing leak on 64-bit hardware and doesn't directly affect cryptographic security."
        },
